HST Office: Word's copy and paste formatting keys, and Ctrl+Q removes paragraph formatting in Writer.

- .uno:HstCopyFormat, .uno:HstPasteFormat (Ctrl+Alt+C, Ctrl+Alt+V; macOS Cmd+Option+C, Cmd+Option+V): the character and
  paragraph formats of the format paintbrush's SwFormatClipboard, without its mouse mode. What the keys copied lives in its
  own instance, so the paintbrush's button and toggle are unaffected, and stays until the next copy.
- .uno:HstResetParagraph (Ctrl+Q on Windows and Linux): the paragraph part of Clear Direct Formatting, keeping page breaks.
  Quit stays on Alt+F4 and in the menu there, on Cmd+Q on macOS. Sheets and Slides keep Ctrl+Q.
- Keys these replace: Insert Comment moves to Ctrl+Alt+M (macOS Cmd+Option+A), Word's keys. Paste Special has no published
  Word key on Windows: Ctrl+Alt+Shift+V, which only repeated Ctrl+Shift+V; macOS Cmd+Control+V, Word's key.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-msoffice-shortcuts.py, docs/SHORTCUTS-MSOFFICE.md.
